FeatherWings for Debian
=======================

FeatherWings is the server control plane for FeatherPanel. It runs as a
systemd service, manages game servers inside Docker, and exposes an HTTP API
and built-in SFTP server for the panel.

Quick start
-----------

1. Install Docker Engine from Docker's official apt repository (required):

   https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/

2. Configure FeatherWings:

       sudo featherwings configure

3. Enable and start the service:

       sudo systemctl enable --now featherwings

Configuration lives in `/etc/featherpanel/config.yml`. The binary is installed
to `/usr/local/bin/featherwings`; a `wings` symlink is created for compatibility
with older scripts.

Channels
--------

- `featherwings` — stable releases (GitHub `v*` tags)
- `featherwings-dev` — per-commit builds from `main`

These packages conflict with each other and cannot be installed together.
Switch channels with apt (the other package is replaced automatically).

Upgrades
--------

Existing configuration is preserved on upgrade. After installing a new version:

       sudo apt-get install --only-upgrade featherwings
       # or
       sudo apt-get install --only-upgrade featherwings-dev

